{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme","id":805787,"title":"Huntsman Scheme?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-10T21:47:41-08:00","id":805787,"title":"Huntsman Scheme?","content":"With the recent release of Huntsman information, my friends and I were wondering about something.<br /> <br /> Since Huntsman will give a token for helping, and will accept a token instead of capturing a changeling, is there anything that prevents a motley of changelings agreeing that one of them will always help the Huntsman (to get the token) and lead them to the target (who hands over the token)? Theoretically they could repeat this process infinitely by passing the token around to whoever the new target is within the motley.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:04:23-08:00","id":805800,"title":"","content":"Scheme assumes there is only ever one Huntsman changelings will have to worry about and that, in the event this is actually the case, a group changelings will have and be confident in this knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T22:21:24-08:00","id":805808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=805800#post805800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scheme assumes there is only ever one Huntsman changelings will have to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Two members of the motley could help two huntsmen, three members could help three huntsman, etc... as long as the number of motley members is twice the number of huntsmen coming after them. And of course if the motley can somehow manage to split the huntsmen group up then they could offer tokens and then exchange the new tokens to dismantle the Huntsman group piecemeal.<br /> <br /> As you mentioned, all of this is contingent upon the motley knowing that some Huntsmen are after them in the first place. But there are two large advantages for a motley attempting to execute this scheme: 1) A storyteller is rarely going to throw a huge amount of Huntsman at a motley without the slightest bit of warning, unless there is some kind of escape avenue open or capture is part of the story. 2) If they do get wind that a Huntsman is coming after one of them, the motley can send someone else to assist them while simultaneously sending vital information back to the motley (such as numbers and targets).<br /> <br /> The biggest complications would not be with the Huntsman (they probably don't care, and just want to get back to Arcadia as fast as possible), but would be situations where the motley knows the Huntsman are coming for them but not who the target is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T23:56:31-08:00","id":805850,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the token wouldn't be in hand until the task is accomplished, the target successfully (and genuinely) betrayed, and the Huntsman is pretty much about to nab your buddy. I mean, sure: some Huntsmen will give tokens for tasks that don't end up in an immediate capture and you could theoretically do this infinitely.<br /> <br /> So what do you do when the task is, &quot;Steal the target Changeling's token&quot;?<br /> <br /> Remember, you have to <i>actually betray your motleymate</i> to get a token. Getting a token for the sake of passing it to him isn't really betrayal anymore, is it?<br /> <br /> I think, if I were a Huntsman, and I encountered this trick, then the next thing I'd do is tell my target that I'm hunting his friend and ask them to go somewhere nice and quiet with me. And then grab them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:21:10-08:00","id":805919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=805850#post805850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the token wouldn't be in hand until the task is accomplished, the target successfully (and genuinely) betrayed, and the Huntsman is pretty much about to nab your buddy. I mean, sure: some Huntsmen will give tokens for tasks that don't end up in an immediate capture and you could theoretically do this infinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording does not seem to suggest genuine betrayal is necessary, only what the Huntsman might consider to be betrayal. A clever huntsman might learn about the scheme, but when returning home with a token is just as good as returning home with your quarry a Huntsman may not actually care.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's possible for an individual Huntsman to pride a successful capture over getting a token, but those would be more limited cases (a storyteller might only be justified bringing such a Huntsman into the story a few times). Most Huntsmen are probably never going to give you a task like &quot;Steal the target Changeling's token&quot; because just taking the token would be far less hassle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:41:11-08:00","id":805927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=805919#post805919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording does not seem to suggest genuine betrayal is necessary, only what the Huntsman might consider to be betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording is less ambiguous about the whole &quot;no token until you do your part&quot; thing, to say nothing of that pesky &quot;getting a token is contingent upon the Huntsman actually making an offer that costs it resources&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:46:51-08:00","id":805931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=805927#post805927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording is less ambiguous about the whole &quot;no token until you do your part&quot; thing, to say nothing of that pesky &quot;getting a token is contingent upon the Huntsman actually making an offer that costs it resources&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Huntsman definitely has to make a bargain in the first place. Though the wording about the kinds of betrayal gives massive leeway about the range of help they can get. And a Huntsman who is basically being offered immediate resolution of his hunt is probably going to be very inclined to accept the offer unless he suspects treachery (which is quite reasonable for the Huntsman to be suspicious about).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:40:28-08:00","id":806006,"title":"","content":"Well, it's something the Huntsman will probably only fall for once, but you could try it, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:49:34-08:00","id":806232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=805931#post805931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a Huntsman who is basically being offered immediate resolution of his hunt is probably going to be very inclined to accept the offer unless he suspects treachery (which is quite reasonable for the Huntsman to be suspicious about).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he, though? Huntsmen may hate existence, but they're still Arcadians, and are therefore bound by the laws of stories. They desire a narratively satisfying hunt just as much as they desire release from existance. It's not really a hunt at all if you're just handed immediate resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:00:04-08:00","id":806244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=806232#post806232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is he, though? Huntsmen may hate existence, but they're still Arcadians, and are therefore bound by the laws of stories. They desire a narratively satisfying hunt just as much as they desire release from existance. It's not really a hunt at all if you're just handed immediate resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say you might be able to pull it off once, though, if only for the narrative impact of a clever twist ending. But fool me once, they say...<br /> <br /> I'd think the real roadblock is the shear level of trust this implies - nothing is stopping the helper-Changeling from just keeping the Token as a guarantee against their own Huntsman. The Prisoner's Dilemma is real, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:32:43-08:00","id":806275,"title":"","content":"Prisoner's Dilemma is certainly a big part of it. Another is that some of the Gentry might enjoy playing along and specifically complicate matters just to see how it all comes crashing down. The more complicated the pile of gambits gets, the more uncertain things are. Uncertainty is a vital part of horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:57:22-08:00","id":806297,"title":"","content":"Note: This assumes a Huntsman decides that giving a Token of Reprieve is worthwhile. They have other, better tools.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'll take a token of reprieve and give you my friend!&quot;<br /> &quot;Nah, I'll just take you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:05:16-08:00","id":806302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=806297#post806297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'll take a token of reprieve and give you my friend!&quot;<br /> &quot;Nah, I'll just take you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiming in to say that while my sentence construction was suboptimal, this is what I meant by &quot;only ever one Huntsman changelings will have to worry about.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:06:50-08:00","id":806303,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I saw that after I posted.<br /> <br /> I really need to remember to read the whole thread.<br /> <br /> But, also worth noting, in relation: Just because the Huntsman has a job to get one person doesn't mean they can't pick up others on the way. It's a little harder, but it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:29:42-08:00","id":806896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805787-huntsman-scheme?p=806303#post806303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I saw that after I posted.<br /> <br /> I really need to remember to read the whole thread.<br /> <br /> But, also worth noting, in relation: Just because the Huntsman has a job to get one person doesn't mean they can't pick up others on the way. It's a little harder, but it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I really like this aspect because I can picture a Huntsmen - one you didn't even know was hunting your friend - appearing in your home, casually unfolding into a nightmarish shape, and asking for your help... with the unspoken implication that if you <i>don't </i>accept its offer, well, it'll take (or kill) you. Betraying someone for a Token is a horrible thing... but not so much, I think, if it's due to an immediate threat to your life. After all, even with your betrayal, your friend still has a chance! Right now, with the Huntsman in your home, do you?<br /> <br /> I also love the text about driving the Hunstman around. It's a wonderful, and horrible, image. The terrified changeling, fully complicit in the ally's hunt, accompanied by the terrifying Huntsman, which forces them to face up to the magnitude of their betrayal, makes it impossible for them to contact and warn their friend... Also, it could easily go full buddy-cop movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:38:05-08:00","id":826416,"title":"","content":"maybe. like eremite said, it doesn't as well if you are coerced into taking to token and forcing someone to take and bringing it up later to someone else seems like something the fae would do to make life harder for the changeling. personally, i would have it work once before the huntsman figures out the trick and uses it to fuck with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}